findings.problem:
The structural classification/drift assertion required by the design is missing. Design lines 87-100 and 446-449 and Issue51 requirement 3 require asserting:
- every named whitelist routing/identity member, CODEX_* and *_PROXY are controls;
- XAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, LANG, TERM, LC_* and XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/XDG_DATA_DIRS are non-control;
- the additional control set is EMPTY.
baseline_key and control are private to this file, and the full file shows only HOME, LC_BAD-NAME, XDG_CONFIG_DIRS and OPENAI_API_KEY being classified.

limitations:
Actual-consumer controls required by the design are not present in the shown sources:
- own-reference edits at each Version/Discovery/Main pre-CAS hook asserting transactional StateConflict and coherent versions;
- own caller-key removal before checkpoint followed by resume initial refusal;
- an own change after checkpoint keeping StateConflict;
- an irrelevant foreign change inside resume's own capture-to-recheck window, so no resume-specific roster-equality mutant credit is evidenced;
- foreign-only LANG/TERM/LC_*/XDG_* conflicts and a shared LANG with own ordinary override reaching the selected child;
- explicit 'still Preparing' assertions after each successful pre-exec CAS.
